WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
A volunteer listens for ten minutes.
A psychologist asks a narrow attention question.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
A screen flashes conflicting arrows.
The task measures responses, not a whole workday.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
The study reports improvements in particular conditions.
It does not test every audio program.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
Now a product page promises twelve minutes can replace an hour.
Where is that direct comparison?

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
Try a free twelve-minute task and write down what actually happened.
Enjoyment is different from proof.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
Read the study. Keep the question.
Don't confuse the recording with the experiment.
